WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:05.005 line:0%
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:24.490 size:78% position:39%
Today, we're near Uvalde,

00:00:24.523 --> 00:00:26.359 align:start position:0%
which is right
in the bottom of Texas.

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:28.394 align:start size:50% position:50%
The more keenly
observant of you

00:00:28.427 --> 00:00:30.563 align:start size:50% position:50%
may have noticed
we're in tank.

00:00:30.596 --> 00:00:33.166 align:start position:0%
I'd be slightly surprised
if you didn't notice the tank,

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.334 align:start size:81% position:19%
- to be fair.
- Yeah, that's fair.

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:38.304 align:start size:84% position:16%
This is an M4 Sherman,
which was built by the U.S.
for World War II.

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:40.239 align:start position:0%
Shall we put it to use,
Daniel?

00:00:40.272 --> 00:00:41.474 align:start size:56% position:44%
I think we should.

00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:43.476 align:start size:28% position:72%
Giddy-up!

00:00:43.509 --> 00:00:45.512
( engine starting )

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.216
Oh!

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.293 align:start position:0%
Here we are.
This is the tank
we're gonna fire.

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.095 align:start position:0%
Slightly different
to the one we were riding in,

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:03.429 align:start position:0%
but it's the same model
of tank, isn't it?

00:01:03.462 --> 00:01:05.198 align:start size:75% position:25% line:0%
Yeah, it's an M4 Sherman
as well,

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:07.200 align:start size:47% position:53% line:0%
but this one's
an "Easy-Eight"
or E8 Sherman.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:10.103 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
It's the only one in existence
that fires and drives.

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:11.404 line:0%
- A rare beast.
- It really is.

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:13.106 align:start size:78% position:22% line:0%
It's got all
the original stuff on it.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.141
<i> All the machine guns on top,
 all original.</i>

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:17.210
- All the fixings.
- All the fixings.

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:19.879 align:start size:56% position:44%
And... we're gonna
be firing this.

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:22.582 align:start size:63% position:38%
15 and a half pounds
of pure solid steal.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:23.783
- Not small.
- Not small.

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:25.751 align:start size:63% position:38%
It's gonna be coming
straight out the end

00:01:25.784 --> 00:01:27.453 align:start size:81% position:19%
of the 76 mil canon there,

00:01:27.486 --> 00:01:30.456 size:84% position:58%
about 2500 foot per second.

00:01:30.489 --> 00:01:32.391 align:start size:91% position:9%
- Gonna need a high-speed
  camera then.
- I think we are.

00:01:32.424 --> 00:01:34.427 align:start position:0%
I feel like we're the right
people for this job.

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:38.764 align:start position:0%
So the tank's over there,
and very handily

00:01:38.797 --> 00:01:41.634 align:start position:0%
at the other end of the range,
is a lovely sort of orange,

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.637
-<i> perforated vehicle. </i>
-<i> Who put that there?</i>

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:46.139 align:start position:0%
That's what we're gonna
be aiming the tank at.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:47.907 align:start position:0%
It's not actually important
that we hit it

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.877 align:start position:0%
because we're mainly interested
in tracking the shell
through the air.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.812 align:start position:0%
But, yeah, it's nice
to have a target.

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:55.715 align:start size:66% position:34%
Oh, for sure.
I mean, the tank has
a range of two miles?

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:58.351
- And that's about 275 yards.
- So, well within its limits.

00:01:58.384 --> 00:01:59.819 align:start size:72% position:28%
- I think so.
- Yeah.

00:01:59.852 --> 00:02:01.787 align:start size:78% position:22%
Considering it goes
at 2,500 feet per second,

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:04.524 align:start size:66% position:34%
I think
it'll get there in...

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.559 align:start size:88% position:13%
- no time at all.
- No time at all, okay.
  Let's go.

00:02:06.592 --> 00:02:07.927 size:78% position:39%
I'm about to fire a tank.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.595 align:start size:56% position:44%
Yeah, not your
everyday activity.

00:02:09.628 --> 00:02:10.796 size:84% position:42%
I wouldn't have thought so.

00:02:10.829 --> 00:02:12.665 align:start size:81% position:19%
- You ready?
- Yeah, let's do it.

00:02:12.698 --> 00:02:13.933 align:start size:53% position:47%
I'm ready
to feel the boom.

00:02:13.966 --> 00:02:17.170 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Okay.
- Three, two, one, fire.

00:02:18.604 --> 00:02:20.606 align:start size:78% position:22%
- Whoa!
- ( chuckles ) Oh!

00:02:20.639 --> 00:02:22.742
That was a real, like, racket.

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.810
My brain was, like, shook.

00:02:24.843 --> 00:02:27.246 align:start size:47% position:53%
It was like
a violent smack

00:02:27.279 --> 00:02:29.615 align:start size:88% position:13%
and then like a nice,
like, whomp in the distance.

00:02:29.648 --> 00:02:30.883 align:start position:0%
A smack and a whomp.

00:02:30.916 --> 00:02:32.685 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Smack and a whomp.
- That was good.

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:34.621 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Satisfying.
- All right, let's see
  what that looked like.

00:02:39.358 --> 00:02:41.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Dan:<i> Whoa. </i>
- Gav:<i> You literally see it.</i>

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:44.897 align:start size:91% position:9%
-<i> Jeez. </i>
-<i> You can see a few frames
 of it there.</i>

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.832
Dan:<i> Oh, yeah.
 It's kind of blurry,</i>

00:02:46.865 --> 00:02:48.634
<i> but you can actually see it.</i>

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:51.337
<i> It just looks
 like a giant bullet.</i>

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.839 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Gav:<i> I guess that's pretty
 much what it is, isn't it? </i>
- Dan:<i> Yeah.</i>

00:02:53.872 --> 00:02:56.309
A giant bullet
from a giant gun.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.477
You ready?

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:01.948
Three, two, one, fire.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.216
Flippin' A.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.284 align:start position:0%
Bugger!

00:03:05.317 --> 00:03:06.786
Whoa!

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:08.321
Oh, man.

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:10.223
So, just before I shot that--

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:11.824 align:start size:81% position:19%
Just before it punched me.

00:03:11.857 --> 00:03:14.660 align:start position:0%
Yeah, just before I shot that,
I'd done my hair right.

00:03:14.693 --> 00:03:16.262 align:start position:0%
It was facing this way.

00:03:16.295 --> 00:03:18.264 align:start position:0%
After I shot it,
it was facing that way.

00:03:18.297 --> 00:03:22.401 align:start size:91% position:9%
- It blew me away.
- Where are your goggles?

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:24.437 align:start position:0%
I was wearing them.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.706 align:start size:69% position:31%
- Were you?
- Yeah.

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:28.675 align:start size:63% position:38%
All right,
let's check Phantom.

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:36.015
Gav:<i> Look at the way the blast
 flaps your sleeve around.</i>

00:03:36.048 --> 00:03:39.018
<i> That was intense.</i>

00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:41.621 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Dan:<i> Wow. </i>
- Gav:<i> Can you see the round?</i>

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.256
Gav:<i> Oh, yeah.</i>

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:44.724
Dan:<i> You can see it,
 a tiny little dot</i>

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.692
<i> sailing off
 into the distance.</i>

00:03:46.725 --> 00:03:48.494
<i> It's quite low.
 It's like against the--</i>

00:03:48.527 --> 00:03:50.496
Gav:<i> Oh, yeah!</i>

00:03:50.529 --> 00:03:52.698
<i> Wow.</i>

00:03:52.731 --> 00:03:54.934 align:start size:91% position:9%
- Did it blow the glasses
  off your face?
- It blew the glasses

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:57.603
<i> ten feet diagonally
 away from me,</i>

00:03:57.636 --> 00:04:00.373
<i> rattled my brain,
 and changed my haircut</i>

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:02.375
all in a split second.

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:04.977 align:start position:0%
Not what you read about
in war books.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.779 align:start size:53% position:47%
No, no, it's not.

00:04:06.812 --> 00:04:08.881 align:start position:0%
One of the things
I'm very excited
about for this video

00:04:08.914 --> 00:04:13.019 align:start position:0%
is that we plan tracking
the tank round through the air.

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.421 align:start position:0%
And I've been using Phantoms
for a long time.

00:04:15.454 --> 00:04:17.056 align:start position:0%
I've been pretty good
at panning.

00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:20.826 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah.
- But I don't think
  I can track by hand

00:04:20.859 --> 00:04:24.830 align:start position:0%
a round that's going, you know,
2,000 feet per second

00:04:24.863 --> 00:04:26.632 align:start position:0%
at 82 feet away.

00:04:26.665 --> 00:04:28.067 align:start size:75% position:25%
I'd like to see you try.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:31.070 align:start position:0%
So, we brought in some big guns
for our big guns.

00:04:31.103 --> 00:04:33.939 align:start position:0% line:0%
This is Frank
from Specialized Imaging.

00:04:33.972 --> 00:04:36.909 align:start position:0% line:0%
Frank, do you want to explain
to us what we've got here
for the Phantom?

00:04:36.942 --> 00:04:40.012
Sure. We have a computer
controlled mirror

00:04:40.045 --> 00:04:42.715
with a high-speed video camera
looking into the mirror.

00:04:42.748 --> 00:04:43.949 align:end position:100%
We don't have to
pan the camera.

00:04:43.982 --> 00:04:46.552 align:start size:56% position:44%
We only have
to pan the mirror.

00:04:46.585 --> 00:04:49.822
And thus we can get these
very fast scan speeds up to,

00:04:49.855 --> 00:04:53.459
in this case, around 2,000
or 3,000 degrees per second.

00:04:53.492 --> 00:04:55.494 align:start size:91% position:9%
- So that means you'd have
  to spin the camera
- Degrees per--

00:04:55.527 --> 00:04:57.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
- 3,000 degrees per second.
- That's how--

00:04:57.796 --> 00:05:00.366 align:start position:0%
- It'd be like...
- It'd be completely impossible

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:02.034 align:start position:0%
with a human muscle,
I assume.

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:03.803 align:start size:78% position:22%
- Correct.
- Unless you drove
  a train into it.

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:05.671 align:start size:81% position:19%
Ten full revs in a second.

00:05:05.704 --> 00:05:06.972 align:start size:75% position:25%
- Yes.
- That's crazy.

00:05:07.005 --> 00:05:09.675
When it's fired,
how does it know when--

00:05:09.708 --> 00:05:12.011
how to turn the camera,
how fast to turn the mirror?

00:05:12.044 --> 00:05:13.946
Sure. The software
that drives the mirror

00:05:13.979 --> 00:05:16.515 align:start size:78% position:22%
allows you to put
in an estimated velocity.

00:05:16.548 --> 00:05:18.484
And we got that
from the gunners here.

00:05:18.517 --> 00:05:22.722
And then we also use two
of our optical trigger systems

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:24.557
looking at the line of flight.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.692
And as the bullet passed
those triggers,

00:05:26.725 --> 00:05:29.662
we actually did an instantaneous
velocity measurement.

00:05:29.695 --> 00:05:31.931
So that means
that you've got two cameras.

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:33.799
The first one sees it,

00:05:33.832 --> 00:05:36.369
and then it measures the time
it takes to get to the next one

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:37.670 align:start size:91% position:9%
- and adjusts the mirror.
- Correct.

00:05:37.703 --> 00:05:39.705 align:start position:0%
So today we're gonna
put the V2512,

00:05:39.738 --> 00:05:43.976 align:start position:0%
pair it with this tracker,
shoot around 28,500
frames a second.

00:05:44.009 --> 00:05:45.578 align:start position:0%
So instead
of panning the camera,

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:47.446 align:start position:0%
the camera stays
perfectly still

00:05:47.479 --> 00:05:48.914 align:start position:0%
and the mirror
does all the work.

00:05:48.947 --> 00:05:51.050 align:start size:72% position:28%
- Ready? Okay.
- Yeah.

00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:54.387
Three, two, one, fire.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.489
Whoa.

00:05:56.522 --> 00:06:00.659 align:start size:75% position:25%
That made a-- that made,
like, a significant
dust pile at the end.

00:06:00.692 --> 00:06:02.395 align:start position:0%
That was a big dust pile,
you're right.

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:03.896 align:start position:0%
- I think that was the biggest.
- Yeah.

00:06:03.929 --> 00:06:06.799 align:start position:0%
Let's go and check out
the tracking shot.

00:06:06.832 --> 00:06:10.169 align:start size:47% position:53%
For reference,
we shot 212,000
pictures there.

00:06:10.202 --> 00:06:12.171
Dan:<i> Whoa.</i>

00:06:12.204 --> 00:06:14.173
<i> Oh! Did you see
 the heat waves there?</i>

00:06:14.206 --> 00:06:16.876
Gav:<i> Flippin'!
 It's outpacing that shockwave.</i>

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:19.044
Dan:<i> Oh, there's a shockwave.
 You can see the shockwave</i>

00:06:19.077 --> 00:06:21.180
-<i> in front of it. </i>
-<i> And behind it.</i>

00:06:21.213 --> 00:06:23.949 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Dan:<i> Whoa! </i>
- Gav:<i> It's trailing a nose--</i>

00:06:23.982 --> 00:06:25.551
<i> Oh, it almost went out
 of frame there.</i>

00:06:25.584 --> 00:06:27.586
<i> So the round is actually
 slightly slower</i>

00:06:27.619 --> 00:06:29.822 align:start size:97% position:3%
-<i> than we wanted to track it. </i>
-<i> That's because it's--</i>

00:06:29.855 --> 00:06:31.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
- It's 'cause it's come out
  like that, though.
- Yeah.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:33.426
It-- Like when
it's actually correct--

00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:35.161
'Cause this is
not supposed to happen.

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:37.530 align:start size:91% position:9%
- See what it's doing?
  You can see it yawing...
- Yeah.

00:06:37.563 --> 00:06:38.798 align:start size:84% position:16%
- ...up and down.
- That's really weird.

00:06:38.831 --> 00:06:42.868
Like that's--
That's "no correct."

00:06:42.901 --> 00:06:45.704
Gav:<i> And obviously it's more
 in focus in the beginning</i>

00:06:45.737 --> 00:06:47.973
<i> than the middle, but then
 it will come back into focus.</i>

00:06:48.006 --> 00:06:50.976 align:start position:0%
-<i> Oh, I was wondering why. </i>
-<i> It's still trailing that wave.</i>

00:06:51.009 --> 00:06:52.878
<i> Look at that.
 There you can see</i>

00:06:52.911 --> 00:06:55.514
<i> there's so much detail in
 the air that's being affected.</i>

00:06:55.547 --> 00:06:57.516
<i> Is it the moisture in the air?
 It must be.</i>

00:06:57.549 --> 00:07:00.119
<i> It looks like exhaust
 from a jet.</i>

00:07:00.152 --> 00:07:01.520
Gav:<i> Love that.</i>

00:07:01.553 --> 00:07:03.856 align:start size:47% position:53%
So I think now,
we should--

00:07:03.889 --> 00:07:05.958 align:start size:88% position:13%
I feel like we've got it.
We know where it's gonna be.

00:07:05.991 --> 00:07:07.693 align:start size:50% position:50%
We should zoom
in a little bit.

00:07:07.726 --> 00:07:09.728
- Oh, go tight. Naughty.
- Go a little bit tighter.

00:07:09.761 --> 00:07:12.898 align:start size:63% position:38%
All right, you ready
for another one?

00:07:12.931 --> 00:07:14.900 align:start position:0%
I-- I am.
I really am.

00:07:14.933 --> 00:07:17.036 align:start size:66% position:34%
All right,
I got Phantom looking
right at your face.

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:18.971 align:start position:0%
I'll try not to look
too dumb then.

00:07:19.004 --> 00:07:20.539 align:start size:88% position:13%
- All right. You ready?
- Yeah.

00:07:20.572 --> 00:07:24.543 align:start position:0%
Okay.
Three, two, one, fire.

00:07:24.576 --> 00:07:26.145 align:start size:75% position:25%
Whoa!

00:07:26.178 --> 00:07:27.980
It smells so good.

00:07:28.013 --> 00:07:29.482
Whoa.

00:07:29.515 --> 00:07:32.651
<i> I look slightly scared
 for a start.</i>

00:07:32.684 --> 00:07:34.820
<i> Shut my eyes like--</i>

00:07:34.853 --> 00:07:37.523
<i> I don't blame you. Ooh!</i>

00:07:37.556 --> 00:07:39.859
<i> ( Gav laughs )</i>

00:07:39.892 --> 00:07:42.027
Dan:<i> Gonna find out exactly
 how far the barrel moves
 back now, as well.</i>

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:43.829
Gav:<i> Oh!</i>

00:07:43.862 --> 00:07:46.565 align:start position:0%
- Gav:<i> Threw out load of gunk. </i>
- Dan:<i> Oh, man.</i>

00:07:46.598 --> 00:07:48.667
Gav:
<i> It significantly jolts back.</i>

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:50.903
Dan:<i> It really does,
 doesn't it?</i>

00:07:50.936 --> 00:07:53.072 align:start size:97% position:3%
-<i> All right, let's go
 and look at the cool shot. </i>
-<i> Okay.</i>

00:07:53.105 --> 00:07:55.074 align:start size:72% position:28%
Now it did have
to lower the frame rate

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:58.210 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Mm-hmm.
- to a measly 12,000
  frames a second.

00:07:58.243 --> 00:08:00.546
- Well, that's pathetic.
- And I widened the shot,

00:08:00.579 --> 00:08:02.715 align:start size:50% position:50%
but we do have
a lot more depth

00:08:02.748 --> 00:08:04.884 align:start size:81% position:19%
to hopefully get much more
of it and focus at once.

00:08:04.917 --> 00:08:06.151 align:start size:75% position:25%
And it's more zoomed in,

00:08:06.184 --> 00:08:08.621 align:start size:66% position:34%
so it's like
a double whammy here.

00:08:08.654 --> 00:08:11.023
Gav:<i> Deliberately set the focus
 to be more in the middle
 of the flight</i>

00:08:11.056 --> 00:08:13.259
<i> so we can see that rifling
 from the side.</i>

00:08:13.292 --> 00:08:15.127
Dan:<i> Mm-hmm. Whoa!</i>

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:19.665
<i> That's really--
 That is so perfectly tracked.</i>

00:08:19.698 --> 00:08:21.233 align:start size:78% position:22%
-<i> That's amazing. </i>
-<i> Look at that.</i>

00:08:21.266 --> 00:08:23.035
<i> Directly in the middle
 of the frame.</i>

00:08:23.068 --> 00:08:25.104
<i>Oh, my word. Oh, you can see it
 spinning there.</i>

00:08:25.137 --> 00:08:26.906
Gav:<i> Yeah, look at that.
 That is the rifling there.</i>

00:08:26.939 --> 00:08:28.607
Dan:<i> Oh, yeah, you can see it
 spinning perfectly.</i>

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:29.975
<i> And as the bow wave as well.</i>

00:08:30.008 --> 00:08:31.644
<i> You see the bow waves
 in the air.</i>

